WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:03.281
(soft music)

00:00:03.283 --> 00:00:04.115
- Hey.

00:00:04.116 --> 00:00:06.116
So uh, Bill’s retirement dinner next week,

00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:07.493
Are you and Anna carpooling?

00:00:07.495 --> 00:00:08.995
- Uh...

00:00:08.996 --> 00:00:10.496
Are me and Anna gonna what?

00:00:10.498 --> 00:00:12.915
- Are you and Anna gonna
carpool straight from work

00:00:12.916 --> 00:00:14.835
to Bill’s retirement dinner?

00:00:14.836 --> 00:00:17.003
- No...

00:00:17.005 --> 00:00:19.881
But we actually broke up.

00:00:19.883 --> 00:00:22.466
So...
- Oh...

00:00:22.468 --> 00:00:23.343
Oh no!

00:00:23.345 --> 00:00:25.178
- Probably not gonna carpool.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.096
- Right.

00:00:27.515 --> 00:00:28.225
Huh.

00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:30.808
God, I am so sorry, man.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:31.768
- It’s okay.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.271
I downloaded Tinder last night.

00:00:35.273 --> 00:00:36.981
I know you’re married.

00:00:36.983 --> 00:00:39.401
Did you just ever go on
there to see how you’d do?

00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:40.943
- No.

00:00:40.945 --> 00:00:41.486
- Right.

00:00:42.821 --> 00:00:46.031
Well anyway, I haven’t filled
out the profile yet, but

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:47.741
it’s there.

00:00:47.743 --> 00:00:48.576
Waiting.
- Good!

00:00:48.578 --> 00:00:49.618
Good for you, man.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.621
Okay, you’re processing
and you’re moving on.

00:00:52.623 --> 00:00:53.331
Good.

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.456
Alright.

00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:55.958
- She was my everything.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.251
- Yeah.

00:00:57.253 --> 00:00:59.963
(office phone rings)

00:00:59.965 --> 00:01:02.506
- You know, we should go out!

00:01:02.508 --> 00:01:03.758
You know?

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.135
Boys night out.

00:01:05.135 --> 00:01:06.761
You, me, Elliot.

00:01:06.763 --> 00:01:08.680
Well not Elliot, but like you and me,

00:01:08.681 --> 00:01:10.015
we go out, we get some drinks,

00:01:10.016 --> 00:01:12.100
we paint the town.

00:01:12.101 --> 00:01:13.478
Look out, ladies!

00:01:14.603 --> 00:01:15.271
- Yeah!

00:01:16.271 --> 00:01:20.275
Yeah, actually tonight though,
tonight is night market

00:01:20.276 --> 00:01:22.110
and let me tell you
about night market, okay?

00:01:22.111 --> 00:01:23.903
So we do it every week, but somehow

00:01:23.905 --> 00:01:25.988
it manages to stay new.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.241
What we do is my wife
and I, we cook dinner,

00:01:28.243 --> 00:01:29.951
a bunch of our couple friends come over,

00:01:29.953 --> 00:01:32.036
somebody brings a bottle of wine,

00:01:32.038 --> 00:01:35.248
and inevitably a spontaneous
game of charades breaks out—

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.208
- Okay, well after that we go get drinks.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.753
- We’re kind in bed early
on school nights, you know?

00:01:40.755 --> 00:01:43.213
(chuckles) Boring married life.

00:01:43.215 --> 00:01:43.841
- Yeah.

00:01:45.468 --> 00:01:47.093
Pretty boring.

00:01:47.095 --> 00:01:48.261
- So how’s Anna?

00:01:48.263 --> 00:01:49.803
- I mean, devastated.

00:01:49.805 --> 00:01:52.015
You know, we were soul mates.

00:01:52.016 --> 00:01:54.350
- So I heard you and Kalyn broke up.

00:01:54.351 --> 00:01:57.186
- Yeah, it had run its course.

00:01:57.188 --> 00:01:58.271
- You doing alright, or...?

00:01:58.273 --> 00:01:59.271
- Could you pass the cream?

00:01:59.273 --> 00:02:00.273
- Oh yeah, here you go.

00:02:00.275 --> 00:02:01.150
- Thank you.

00:02:02.235 --> 00:02:04.526
- So that’s why I’m gonna
award the Nether’s account

00:02:04.528 --> 00:02:05.986
to Kalyn!

00:02:05.988 --> 00:02:08.155
- You’re giving the adult
toy account to Kalyn?

00:02:08.156 --> 00:02:10.324
- Yeah, Kalyn is carefree, he’s playful,

00:02:10.326 --> 00:02:13.118
who better to lead an
account specializing in toys

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.578
for adults?

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.913
- Do you know what
adult toys are, Natalie?

00:02:15.915 --> 00:02:17.873
- Yeah, I mean, bikes for two,

00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:19.458
gin rummy, billiards.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:22.795
Anyway, Anna, I want you to
be second chair on this one.

00:02:22.796 --> 00:02:24.130
- Great choice, Natalie.

00:02:24.131 --> 00:02:26.298
I really think Elliot is gonna be

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.216
the perfect second chair on this one.

00:02:28.218 --> 00:02:30.636
- I actually said Anna, not Elliot.

00:02:30.638 --> 00:02:32.430
- I think we all know that Elliot

00:02:32.431 --> 00:02:35.516
would be the perfect choice
for the Nether’s account.

00:02:35.518 --> 00:02:37.060
- No, nobody thinks that.

00:02:37.061 --> 00:02:39.645
- Great, I’m glad it’s settled.

00:02:39.646 --> 00:02:40.898
Welcome aboard, Elliot.

00:02:43.776 --> 00:02:46.235
(office phone ringing)

00:02:46.236 --> 00:02:49.821
- Hey, I’m sorry I took
your place on Nether’s.

00:02:49.823 --> 00:02:53.158
I don’t know why Kalyn thinks
I’m some sort of sex expert.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.535
Probably my musk.

00:02:54.536 --> 00:02:56.370
- Kalyn is just processing our breakup.

00:02:56.371 --> 00:02:57.330
- You guys broke up?

00:02:57.331 --> 00:02:59.081
- Yeah, last night.

00:02:59.083 --> 00:03:02.001
- Well didn’t he just meet your parents?

00:03:02.003 --> 00:03:04.130
- That was regrettable,
but we all make mistakes.

00:03:05.881 --> 00:03:08.215
Big mistakes.

00:03:08.216 --> 00:03:10.510
- But I can assure you
it won’t affect our work.

00:03:10.511 --> 00:03:11.803
We’re both professionals.

00:03:11.805 --> 00:03:14.805
- You know Anna calls sex “bedtime” ?

00:03:14.806 --> 00:03:16.808
Do you know how confusing that is?

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:17.808
- We’re actually talking about

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.310
Bill’s retirement party right now.

00:03:19.311 --> 00:03:20.436
- Right.

00:03:20.438 --> 00:03:23.105
- I can’t even believe he’s retiring.

00:03:23.106 --> 00:03:26.025
- Anna has this mole on,
like, the small of her back,

00:03:26.026 --> 00:03:27.943
and I’ve been taking
pictures of it to make sure

00:03:27.945 --> 00:03:30.113
it’s not changing shape;

00:03:30.115 --> 00:03:31.698
who’s gonna monitor it now, you know?

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:32.575
Not me!

00:03:34.118 --> 00:03:36.703
(groans) Not me.

00:03:36.705 --> 00:03:39.913
- Kalyn, can we talk?

00:03:39.915 --> 00:03:41.250
- Sure.

00:03:45.171 --> 00:03:46.628
- I wonder what the mole looks like.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.213
- Bill’s retirement
party, are you driving?

00:03:48.215 --> 00:03:49.840
I need a ride.

00:03:49.841 --> 00:03:51.133
- Do you want to get back together?

00:03:51.135 --> 00:03:52.051
- No!

00:03:52.053 --> 00:03:54.595
Hey, I just want to discuss
remaining professional

00:03:54.596 --> 00:03:55.971
in the workplace.

00:03:55.973 --> 00:03:59.766
- Did I mean anything to you?

00:03:59.768 --> 00:04:00.728
- What?

00:04:02.063 --> 00:04:04.980
Please just pull yourself together, okay?

00:04:04.981 --> 00:04:07.233
This job is important to me.

00:04:07.235 --> 00:04:09.318
- Cold as ice.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.405
Must be nice to not care
about anything, huh?

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:19.952
- Oh, you guys want to carpool to Bill’s

00:04:19.954 --> 00:04:21.120
retirement dinner next week?

00:04:21.123 --> 00:04:21.956
- Yes!

00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:22.750
Finally.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:26.085
- I’m gonna miss Bill.

00:04:26.086 --> 00:04:28.588
We used to have cat play-dates every week.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.383
Next week we were gonna go to Legoland.

00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:42.561
(soft music)

00:05:02.206 --> 00:05:05.403
(orchestral music)

